From: BoxDroid downstream
Subject: [PATCH] tcg/aarch64: exact ordered scalar RAM lowering

Use LDAPR (when supported), otherwise LDAR, and STLR for aligned scalar RAM.
Unaligned RAM stays inline with ordinary accesses and exact barriers. Bridge ordinary reads at
C execution entries. Unknown helpers, slow scalar loads, store-helper RAM
reads and vector loads complete with an acquire barrier. All helpers retain cpu_req_mo();
MMIO, faults, unaligned and 128-bit accesses retain conservative handling.
Audited CPU-state-only x87 helpers preserve the acquire region.
Never infer exclusive RAM ownership from !CF_PARALLEL.

